{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQ8Z1FmiZr1pJP1d3JhW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"In fiscal 2024, Airbnb added back **$1.407 billion** ($1,407 million) of stock-based compensation expense in its cash flow statement. This is the non-cash adjustment used to reconcile net income to cash from operating activities.\n\nFor comparison, the 2023 figure was $1.120 billion, so the 2024 amount was about 26% higher.\n\nThe value comes from the XBRL tag ShareBasedCompensation (\"Share-based Payment Arrangement, Noncash Expense\") in Airbnb's FY2024 10-K. A filing dated after 16 May 2025 also turned up in the results, so I didn't use it.\n\n**Sources**\n- Airbnb, Inc. Form 10-K for FY2024, filed 2025-02-13, accession 0001559720-25-000010 (XBRL financial data)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":797,"cache_read_input_tokens":7742,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":797},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cc0190d5-57b1-4e3e-9728-abb2735c8e42","uuid":"a7fa1498-bbce-48ec-93dd-6e638f5870d7","timestamp":"2026-10-26T03:22:38.980Z","request_id":"req_011CgQ8Yzz9G9sSkoYdipste"}
